  "help_subtitle": "Short guides to get the most out of Wumbi.",
  "help_tags_title": "How to use tags?",
  "help_tags_subtitle": "Labels, nested tags and the map",
  "help_tags_intro": "Tags are short labels like #coffee that you add to transactions. A transaction can carry several tags, so you can look at your money from any angle — not only by wallet.",
  "help_tags_add_title": "Add a tag",
  "help_tags_add_body": "When you enter a transaction, type a name in the tags field, then pick a suggestion or create a new one. Tags have no spaces — write coffee-shop or coffee_shop. Upper and lower case give the same tag.",
  "help_tags_nested_title": "Nested tags",
  "help_tags_nested_body": "Use a slash / to put a tag inside another one, like folders: food/coffee and food/groceries both live inside food. The parent tag is created for you.",
  "help_tags_parent_title": "A parent includes its nested tags",
  "help_tags_parent_body": "Opening #food shows every transaction tagged #food, #food/coffee or #food/groceries. Totals, filters and budgets on a parent count its nested tags too. A transaction with both tags is counted only once.",
  "help_tags_multi_title": "Several tags on one transaction",
  "help_tags_multi_body": "A dinner on holiday can be #travel and #food/restaurant at the same time. It then counts in both, and the two tags get linked on the map.",
  "help_tags_manage_title": "Create, rename, move",
  "help_tags_manage_body": "On the Tags page, tap + to create a tag and pick a parent to nest it. Open a tag to rename it, move it under another parent, add a nested tag or delete it. Renaming a parent renames its nested tags; renaming into an existing tag merges the two.",
  "help_tags_map_title": "Read the map",
  "help_tags_map_body": "Every circle is a tag: the bigger it is, the more money it moved. Its ring shows the share of spending and income. Solid lines join a parent to its nested tags, faint lines join tags used on the same transaction. Tap a circle to see its numbers.",
  "help_tags_tips_title": "Tips",
  "help_tags_tip1": "Start broad — food, home, transport — and nest only when you want more detail.",
  "help_tags_tip2": "Use tags for what cuts across wallets: #vacation, #gifts, #car.",
  "help_tags_tip3": "Keep names short; two or three levels are plenty.",
  "help_tags_example": "Example",
  "help_tags_example_total": "Total for #food",
